// =============================================================================
// Go workspace.
//
// WHY A WORKSPACE RATHER THAN ONE MODULE:
//
// Each service is its own module with its own go.mod. That means each service
// declares only the dependencies it actually uses, so an unrelated dependency
// upgrade in `billing` cannot force a rebuild or a security review of
// `media-relay`. It also keeps service container images minimal, because the
// build context for one service does not drag in the dependency graph of eight.
//
// The workspace then stitches those modules together for local development, so
// an engineer editing packages/go/platform sees the change reflected in every
// consuming service immediately, with no version bump ceremony.
//
// ON THE `replace` DIRECTIVES IN EACH SERVICE go.mod:
//
// Each service additionally carries a relative-path `replace` for the shared
// platform module. That is deliberate and, for now, necessary. This repository
// is private and unpublished, so the module path above is not fetchable; in
// workspace mode Go still needs a resolvable version for every module in the
// build list in order to compute go.work.sum, and without the replace it
// attempts a network fetch that fails — taking unrelated modules down with it.
//
// The replace also keeps each module buildable standalone with GOWORK=off,
// which CI relies on to prove that a module's go.mod is genuinely
// self-sufficient rather than quietly leaning on the workspace to resolve
// something.
//
// These directives are removed once the repository is published and the module
// path resolves on its own. Until then they are load-bearing, not legacy.
// =============================================================================

go 1.25.0

use (
	./packages/go/audiobridge
	./packages/go/voice
	./packages/go/audiointel
	// Generated protobuf and Connect RPC bindings. Never hand-edited; produced
	// by `task contracts:generate` and drift-checked in CI.
	./packages/go/contracts-go
	./packages/go/correlation
	./packages/go/conversation
	./packages/go/evalstore
	./packages/go/evalsubjects
	./packages/go/evaluation
	./packages/go/eventbus
	./packages/go/governance
	./packages/go/integrations
	./packages/go/media
	./packages/go/memory
	./packages/go/metrics
	./packages/go/metricsexport
	./packages/go/middleware
	./packages/go/outbox
	./packages/go/persistence
	./packages/go/platform
	./packages/go/redis
	./packages/go/repository
	./packages/go/runtime
	./packages/go/speech
	./packages/go/telemetry
	./packages/go/telephony
	./packages/go/toolruntime
	./services/go/analytics
	./services/go/billing
	./services/go/cognitive-reasoning
	./services/go/compliance
	./services/go/consumer
	./services/go/contacts-sync

	// Services
	./services/go/edge-api
	./services/go/family
	./services/go/fraud-detection
	./services/go/identity
	./services/go/media-relay
	./services/go/notification-fanout
	./services/go/session-orchestrator
	./services/go/speech-streaming
	./services/go/telephony-gateway
	./services/go/voice
)
